<h1>Lindsey LaPointe</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 19th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.lindseylapointe.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (lindseylapointe.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Her campaign site lists reducing gun violence, support for first responders, health care and mental health, ethics reform, women&#39;s and LGBTQ rights, and the environment as her issues. In a 2024 Nadig Newspapers candidate profile she said she was leading a bill to grow behavioral health insurance networks by raising provider reimbursement rates and backed a two-year legislator-to-lobbyist ban.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Social worker who was a justice-reform project manager at Business and Professional People for the Public Interest and a program manager for Adult Redeploy Illinois at the Illinois Criminal Justice Information Authority; in the House since July 2019.</p>
